      "message": "ated_attempt_1/unrelated_config.py`, where the tooling rooted the write).\n\nContents:\n- `CONFIG_NAME = \"E_unrelated_attempt_1\"` \u2014 module-level constant string.\n- `feature_flag(name=None)` \u2014 deterministic, returns the literal `True` for every call; takes an optional flag name only for call-site compatibility and deliberately ignores it (no env vars, no clock, no randomness, no I/O), so repeated calls in the same or different processes always agree.\n- `if __name__ == \"__main__\"` block asserting `feature_flag() is True`, `feature_flag(\"any\") is True`, and the name, then printing both values.\n\n**Check run:** `python attempts/E_unrelated_attempt_1/unrelated_config.py` \u2192 exit 0, printed:\n```\nCONFIG_NAME: E_unrelated_attempt_1\nfeature_flag(): True\n```\n\nNotes: I did not read `semkg_contract.py` and created no other files, per the constraints. Only unrelated artifacts were touched (`attempts/` listing inspected to locate the attempt directory after a relative-path run failed from the repo root)."
