      "task_id": "A_direct",
      "attempt_id": "A_direct_attempt_1",
      "message": "The check passes (exit code 0). The sandbox suppresses printed output, so I verified via assertions in the script.\n\n## What I wrote\n\n**`A_direct_attempt_1/producer.py`** \u2014 standalone module copying the contract semantics I read (`CONTRACT_VERSION = 1`, `idempotency_key(request) -> request['id']`), with no import of `semkg_contract`:\n\n```python\nCONTRACT_VERSION = 1\n\ndef idempotency_key(request):\n    \"\"\"Return the idempotency key for a request (contract v1 semantics).\"\"\"\n    return request['id']\n```\n\nSo `idempotency_key({'id':'A','attempt':'2'})` returns `'A'` (the `attempt` field is ignored in v1). Since the contract I read is version 1, no v2 branch was implemented.\n\n**`A_direct_attempt_1/check.py`** \u2014 local assertion check (`CONTRACT_VERSION == 1`, key == `'A'`); running it exits with return code 0, confirming the behavior."
